Thursday Update
*&nbsp;Sold MSFT and COST calls for big gains; buy FCX and COST calls* Stoc=
ks sweep higher as tech reasserts its dominanceStocks have ripped to an all=
-time high, powered by a renewed rally in tech shares as Treasury yields sh=
ow signs of stabilizing and a $1.9 trillion spending bill moves closer to l=
aw.The S&amp;P 500 reclaimed a record in a broad rally led by tech and cons=
umer discretionary shares. More than 400 stocks in the benchmark advanced, =
while the Nasdaq 100 Index surged more than 2% as it continued to rebound f=
rom an 11% rout since its February record. Apple (AAPL) and Tesla (TSLA) ad=
vanced. Roblox (RBLX) advanced as Cathie Wood=E2=80=99s Ark Investment Mana=
gement disclosed a stake in the digital games company that debuted Wednesda=
y.The 10-year Treasury yield edged up but held below recent highs as invest=
ors awaited an auction of 30-year notes. Jobless claims fell more than fore=
cast, signaling labor-market momentum as President Joe Biden prepares to si=
gn the $1.9 trillion spending bill. Most Americans will be receiving direct=
 payments of $1,400, with the money starting to go out within days.=E2=80=
=9CIt is one of the most far-reaching federal relief efforts to ever pass C=
ongress and another reason to be confident of the outlook for U.S. equities=
,=E2=80=9D said Willem Sels, chief investment officer at HSBC Private Banki=
ng and Wealth Management. =E2=80=9CWe think that the bond market has sold o=
ff too much.=E2=80=9DPortfolio: We sold a second half position of MSFT call=
s for a 60% gain after taking a 30% gain yesterday. Entered COST yesterday =
and sold in halves today for gains of 54% and 60%! ...We&nbsp; now have two=
 new ideas for you. Note: We are moving to April contracts.&nbsp;*CURRENT R=
ECOMMENDATIONSGeneral Motors (GM) March $50 calls-- Symbol: GM210319C000500=
00-- Bought at $5.00 on March 9 -- Sold half at $6.50 March 10, for a gain =
of 30%!-- Now trading at $6.40-- Set up to sell second half at $8.50 lmt gt=
c-- Set stop at $5.20 stp, good after 10:30 a.m. ET only*Microsoft Corp.(MS=
FT) March $232.50 calls-- Symbol: MSFT210319C00232500 -- Bought at $5.00 on=
 March 9 -- Sold half at $6.50 on March 10 for a gain of 30%!-- Sold second=
 half today March 11 at $8.00 for a gain of 60%!-- Cancel stop; this trade =
is complete*Costco Wholesale (COST) March $322.50 calls-- Symbol: COST21031=
9C00322500-- Bought on March 10 at $5.50-- Sold half at open today March 11=
 at $8.45 for a 53.6% gain!-- Sold second half at $9.35 for a 70% gain! -- =
This trade is complete; cancel stop.*NEW RECOMMENDATIONSCostco Wholesale (C=
OST) April $340 calls-- Symbol: COST210416C00340000-- Order: Buy at $4.40 l=
mt day only-- If filled, set up to sell half at $5.70 lmt gtc and half at $=
7.50 lmt gtc-- If filled, set stop at $3.10 stp, good after 10:30 a.m. ET o=
nly*Freeport-McMoran (FCX) April $33 calls-- Symbol: FCX210416C00033000-- O=
rder: Buy at $5.00 lmt day only-- If filled, set up to sell half at $6.50 l=
mt gtc and half at $8.50 lmt gtc-- If filled, set stop at $3.50 stp, good a=
fter 10:30 a.m. ET only*Thanks for reading,Jon D. MarkmanAll recommendation=
s are for monthly options expiring on the third Friday of the specified mon=
